{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346489-fighting-the-technocracy-in-service-of-a-mage","id":1346489,"title":"Fighting the Technocracy in service of a Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-06T09:47:36-08:00","id":1346489,"title":"Fighting the Technocracy in service of a Mage?","content":"(I was initially going to post this question on W:TO, but this forum seems more active)<br /> <br /> So theoretically a Mage uses Spirit to evoke your character to have a passion [Serve Master X (5)] and orders you to fight the Technocracy, how would a Wraith fare against the fighting against the Technocracy? Reading the 2nd Edition of M:TA it says that Effect attacks that are seen whether coincidental or vulgar can be dodged with a regular Dex + Dodge. What about more abstract things like a Mind 3 to cause the Wraith to go insane or some Matter Effect (since Wraith's are solidified raw emotion), can it use Willpower to resist such a thing? This is all under the assumption the Wraith is Embodied fighting the Technocrats<br /> <br /> Also since Technocrats (except for VE) don't focus on Spirit at all, can an experienced combat base Wraith clean up house of a Technocrat Lab/Installation? Assuming the Void Engineers aren't called in of course. Note aswell that due to the Passion and the Wraith doing objectives to take down the Technocratic machinations are purview of its master, it would be getting a 5 dice chance everytime to gain more Pathos to fuel Arcanoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-06-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:30:49-08:00","id":1346503,"title":"","content":"Saying all technocrats except for the VE don't focus on dimensional science is a bit of a misnomer. There are NWO observers who study the paranormal after all. It's possible to just use correspondence \\Spirit to create a ward that will fry the little ghost before it can even enter the facility","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:43:25-08:00","id":1346504,"title":"","content":"Is there any possible way for a Wraith to resist that? What about Fatalism of 5?<br /> <br /> Edit: Also don't Technocrats almost always need Foci and don't (but can't because its against their philosophy) use Vulgar magic? What possible ward out of nowhere could an Agent use to stop a very combat or stealth oriented Wraith from getting close to the Installation (Satellite, coincidental Turrent, etc.?)? Beside VE, I thought Technocrats don't use Spirit that much - and if they do, they only ever have it at 1. With an &quot;influence&quot; (Sphere) that low, they would only be able to sense if very close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":".  Vulgar Magic and Foci? 11-06-2019, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T10:49:13-08:00","id":1346507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346489-fighting-the-technocracy-in-service-of-a-mage?p=1346504#post1346504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any possible way for a Wraith to resist that? What about Fatalism of 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know nothing about that, however the technocracy is nothing but adaptable. While the wraith might trash a place once it would be much harder to do so a second time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:18:20-08:00","id":1346517,"title":"","content":"Myes. The Wraith might quite possibly be able to suprise the technocrats the first time - generally speaking, the Technos don't tend to have Ghost problems on their home turf on average, simply because hauntings there are probably exceedingly rare in the first place.<br /> <br /> That said, it also depends on what kind of technocratic facility we are talking about. Just some offices acting as a front for a cabal? A military instalation that hides out some serious Hypertech experimentations? The question wether or not the Wraith will be able to wreak havoc highly, *highly* depends on what the actual target is.<br /> <br /> Also, the Matter sphere won't apply - Wraiths emotions are covered by the Mind sphere. Now, one thing that shouldn't be overlooked is the *Prime* sphere. Prime - or rather the force it controls - is the the very building block of reality. If the wraith crosses the shroud and is actually present in the real world, Prime *will* be able to damage it. Nastily so. And the Prime sphere is not restricted at all; NWO agents or Iterators with prime-charged ammunitions might be a threat.<br /> But again - the presence of the same once more depends on the installation in question.<br /> <br /> So, going through some of the appropriate spheres,<br /> <br /> * Dimensional Science/Spirit - Mostly in the hands of VEs, but yes, there are exceptions; Still, the chance of encountering it is way lower than Technocrats wielding other enlightened sciences.<br /> * Mind - Actually probably a BIG danger here, as the NWO specializes in this through and through, and NWO agents are never far in technocratic locations - unless it is a location mostly held by a single Convention, like a Progenitor lab.<br /> * Prime - There's always a chance of encountering this across the board. In a combat scenario, in the form of aformentioned charged special ammunitions most likely. However, such ammo is costly in terms of Quintessence, so definitely for 'special situations' and accordingly restricted - unless the Wraith crosses a member of the Syndicate. Don't let the mobster pull out their Little Friend.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Actually, the best strategy for the Wraith is to take it *slow*. Like days. Weeks. Don't go full on 'Freaky ghost terror'. Be subtle. Cause accidents. Cause malfunctions at the worst of times. Depending on how much the Wraith knows about the details of the Technocracy (Chance is next to zero unless their Mystic master tells them...) the Wraith can use the paranoia of the NWO *against* them. Listen in. Find out which of the Technocrats might be rivals. Cause accidents that seem like one offed another. Focus on single targets and slowly whittle down their resolve. Do not make it obvious that a haunting is taking place unless when its time to release the brakes, and then make a hasty exit and let the Technocrats scramble to figure out what happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-06-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:28:24-08:00","id":1346522,"title":"","content":"So basically the Wraith should only start ambushing targets with low Arete (not that a Wraith would know the Arete level, but just /knowing/ that the Technocrat is a &quot;grunt&quot;) say a mere 2 or 1, they could clock such an field operative after Embodying with a Soulsteel weapon easily right? Mages in MTA can't have a sphere above their Arete level right? <br /> <br /> How long could a Wraith begin killing off low-level operatives (say Watchers from the NWO who report Reality Deviations) before they send the big shots after it? Also can you inform what a Wraith can do to resist a Mind Effect? Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T19:33:05-08:00","id":1346639,"title":"","content":"A mages highest sphere is capped by their Arete, yes.<br /> <br /> &quot;How long could a Wraith begin killing off low-level operatives (say Watchers from the NWO who report Reality Deviations) before they send the big shots after it? Also can you inform what a Wraith can do to resist a Mind Effect? Willpower?&quot;<br /> <br /> The issue is it depends on how they die. The Technocracy probably has cameras on alot of things, and those cameras may have spirit sight 'Extradimensional sight or some shit', that might catch a spooky ghost in action. Even 1 strange death would be enough to have some agent stop by with a fancy machine/time magick to see what the fuck actually happened.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T05:48:24-08:00","id":1346701,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a><br /> \u200b<br /> 1\u00ba Let's cleanse some misconceptions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So don't Technocrats almost always need Foci. </div> </div> </div>Yes. Always<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and don't (but can't because its against their philosophy) use Vulgar magic? </div> </div> </div>They can and do use Vulgar magick, but will try not to. They have no more limitations here than Traditionalists, but it won't look good on their reports. Especially if it's in front of witnesses, &quot;masquerade breaches&quot; are as serious deal within the Technocracy as within the Camarilla<br /> <br /> The thing is: Vulgar magick may not be Vulgar inside a Construct/Chantry because it most likely counts as a Reality Zone (and even if it *was* Vulgar, it likely won't be a &quot;masquerade breache&quot; there).<br /> <br /> Moreso, frying a Wraith in the Dark Umbra/Shadowlands isn't Vulgar because most magick casted within the Umbra (even if the mage it's casting *from* earth) it's Coincident.<br /> <br /> If you want to take advantage of Vulgarity you would need to Materialize (and even then it may not work inside their instalations)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What possible ward out of nowhere could an Agent use to stop a very combat or stealth oriented Wraith from getting close to the Installation (Satellite, coincidental Turrent, etc.?)? </div> </div> </div>Any &quot;science looking&quot; stuff would do. It doesn't <i>need</i> to look common unless it's to be used outside. It will likely be a machine of some sorts, but it doesn't <i>need </i>to be, a bureucratic memo could do it if the Ward was made by those rare NWO agents who have mastered DimSci. In general, Foci are too versatile to be called a weakness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beside VE, I thought Technocrats don't use Spirit that much - and if they do, they only ever have it at 1. </div> </div> </div>Levels 1 and 2 aren't *terribly* uncommon outside VE. Only the ItX were forbidden from learning it (and in Revised that law was lifted), the rest just don't care much about it, hence they rarely learn more than a few levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With an &quot;influence&quot; (Sphere) that low, they would only be able to sense if very close. </div> </div> </div>Sphere levels at 1 can detect anything in the range of sight. Combined with Correspondence 1+ they can detect anything in very, very, large areas. Because Corr isn't rare at all, you can't really take this for granted. <hr /><br /> If this was a really OP or easy tactic against them, Dreamspeakers would have obliterated the Technocracy long ago. The fact that Dreamspeakers, Euthanatos and other EDE-using mages hate the guts of the Technocracy means that summoning entities only affected by DimSci (like a wraith) to haunt their bases isn't unheard off. There's probably a protocol for that in most Constructs.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that the technocracy it's a Union. Technocrats are rarely so broad in their powers as Tradition mages, but they compensate this by relying on other mages. Technocrats &quot;in general&quot; may not have DimSci, but VE work day and night to protect all Constructs from such &quot;extradimensional&quot; attacks. Even if they aren't there *personally*, there could be Wards, special cameras or other items to deal with this problem<br /> <br /> And that's where Ambrosia's statement really comes into play:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question wether or not the Wraith will be able to wreak havoc highly, *highly* depends on what the actual target is.</div> </div> </div> </div>A powerful Construct or any one that was intended to fight the Traditions will be hard for a Wraith to infiltrate. That place it's going to have VE OR VE-tech to protect against this kind of incursion because Traditionalists DO this thing a lot, and thus it would be impossible for them to survive w/o propper EDE defenses<br /> <br /> A recent/low level Construct or one that wasn't intended for the Ascencion War <u>MAY </u>not have strong anti-EDE protections. This is the ideal target for a slow, subtle, infiltration where you pit one Techncorat against the other. If you start &quot;misteriously&quot; killing people, it's not going to last long until someone calls the VE.<br /> <br /> A front where most of the operatives are human?. Feel free to camp there as much as you want. However, again, if people starts having gruesome deaths the larger Union WILL appear to cleanse the place.<br /> <br /> In general, a haunting on a Technocracy base it's not going to last long (more or less will depend on how careful you are about revealing your presence, and the kind of attacks Technocrats expect), but perhaps small acts of sabotage or a sudden, strong and quick surprise attack it's all that you need to do in order to fulfill the desires. Because most Technoctats DO have a blind spot there, it's likely that you can get away with it (at least once).<br /> <br /> That being said, I recomend not to be overconfident. These are mages, in the hand of STs that's basically &quot;plot devices&quot;: If the ST wants to screw you with them, he has every tool to do so within the rules. <hr />As for strategies:<br /> Techncorats themselves <u>may </u>be too protected by Mind to make puppets of them (NWO sure are), but most likely the mundane/sorcerous staff isn't protected, and they actions would be less monitored.<br /> <br /> It may be worth to note you *can* Inhabit Devices (not sure if it would work on conscious devices like the Hit-Mark, though)<br /> <br /> Fatalism it's subtle, and that's good for many strategies (can be countered/detected with Entropy, though) but unless W20 made changes or you're using a Fatalism 5 power I don't know, my understanding it's that what Fatalism 5 does has little to do with Wards. Maybe a very good roll with Argos could be used as &quot;countermagic&quot; for Wards (though RAW countering a ritual it's nigh impossible. But if I was ST I would make so you can give a shot). Still, let's not assume a Ward until we see one. Sometimes you don't need to pick a lock to open a door.<br /> <br /> Your best strategy may be to try to be subtle within their instalations, and only try to kill Technocrats when they go outside (preferably in ways that would seem like an accident, bonus points if they look like an accident from the PoV of a Time user too). The less they know, the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-07-2019, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T06:19:11-08:00","id":1346710,"title":"","content":"That's the other thing you're misunderstanding. Thanks to institutional preference for gadgets, Gizmos, and Wonders.... Chances are it's not just the mages you need to worry about. Joe the Agent with an Arete of 0 can use the Hypertech Extradimensional security system all on his own to detect dimensional Intruders.<br /> <br /> Could it be effective in certain facilities? Certainly. But anything but the lightest of defended facilities could have any number of defenses. For example, could be that as far as the wraith can tell the facility doesn't exist on the other side. Like good old Number 12 Grimmauld Place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T07:22:29-08:00","id":1346720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346489-fighting-the-technocracy-in-service-of-a-mage?p=1346710#post1346710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the other thing you're misunderstanding. Thanks to institutional preference for gadgets, Gizmos, and Wonders.... Chances are it's not just the mages you need to worry about. Joe the Agent with an Arete of 0 can use the Hypertech Extradimensional security system all on his own to detect dimensional Intruders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> It *needs* to be stressed out that &quot;only&quot; VE having DimSci by no means imply that only VE are dangerous. Technocrats are developers, industrials...well...technocrats. VE &quot;produce&quot; a kind of tech that can be used to counter ghosts. After that, &quot;anyone&quot; (with special training) can use it. Including normal humans and other Convention agents. Not to mention that they can build autonomous defense system do not even need to be used.<br /> <br /> That being said, it's pretty much stated that gadgets are still valuable. And VE gadgets are rarer than most. It's unlikely that the security guy on the front door has an EDE-disruptor at hand at all times. They probably would need to requisition one (like most agents).<br /> <br /> It also may be argued that gadgets attuned with the Shadowlads <i>may be somewhat less common ..</i>. Wraiths / Agama wizards being less common of a treath than the Astral/Middle Umbra types (and Haunts being more common in ruined, entropic, places) ... I could see a low security base neglecting this layer to some extent. Especially one not personally secured by the VE. Still, it's not something one can really count on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-07-2019, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:30:06-08:00","id":1346734,"title":"","content":"It only takes me like 20 minutes to put an order in for some fucking ghost sunglasses and a case of prime bullets to tell any wraith to fuck right off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:02:05-08:00","id":1346777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346489-fighting-the-technocracy-in-service-of-a-mage?p=1346734#post1346734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It only takes me like 20 minutes to put an order in for some fucking ghost sunglasses and a case of prime bullets to tell any wraith to fuck right off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are like 200-400 combat turns. Start practicing to do it in 5' :P<br /> <br /> Or don't, any place worth protecting should have an armory with some Primium bullets and special sunglesses. You can sign the papers afterwards.<br /> <br /> Still you have to be alive to *get* there, and that's when one really starts appreciating Correspondence...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-07-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:05:25-08:00","id":1346827,"title":"","content":"Prime Sphere (or influence' by ways to the Technocracy) makes any weapon, unarmed, or regular object be imbued with Quintessence right? Wraiths can soak Aggrevated damage naturally and being prepped with looted Stygian Armor or a Soul-based Armor made by the Master for the Wraith can easily ward off those dangerous Primium bullets... I'd only be very scared of a VE-Tech though- who knows what can they do.. Now that I think about it, I agree- a Wraith would only have to target personnel on field missions really. Trying to solo a construct by yourself is suicide and some big dumb-assery. Though I still think people over-state the power of Mages through. Yeah they are extremely powerful Reality Warpers, but they are still bound by Paradox. If I'm battling a Mage or &quot;Enlightened&quot; individual, if they botch a roll Paradox can off them for you. <br /> <br /> What if the binded Wraith had a large Shadowland warband (Renegade Host who does not care for the Dictuum Mortium) at his disposal- say the Mage specifically sought to bind the Wraith for that very reason, what level of Construct/Installation could I take out? <br /> <br /> Also I got another question about Mages in general- if they fail an Arete roll, does that cause a Paradox backlash? Or do backlashes only happen with a botch? Also if it is a fail and no botch, does that cause Paradox even if it was a coincidental Effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:35:34-08:00","id":1346838,"title":"","content":"1. Technocracy refers to quintessence as Primal energy but the sphere retains the name. <br /> <br /> 2. Keep in mind a technocracy lab/construct is considered a sanctum so everything there is coincidental when it comes to generating paradox.<br /> <br /> Backlashes occur when you generate enough paradox points to trigger one ( 5points in M20)<br /> Depends on what edition you are using for point generation though. <br /> <br /> While prime does do aggravated damage it also costs points in quintessence to do so. Adding spirit 2 to a forces effect will also do some damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":". 11-07-2019, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T05:38:44-08:00","id":1346987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I still think people over-state the power of Mages through. Yeah they are extremely powerful Reality Warpers, but they are still bound by Paradox. If I'm battling a Mage or &quot;Enlightened&quot; individual, if they botch a roll Paradox can off them for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <i>Dwight </i>(and I, previously) mentioned, Vulgarity it's not going to be your friend when you get inside the Construct. And one can't really count on Botches on a fight, they're not that frequent, and depending on several factors the effect may not be powerful enough to matter right away. This is true for all combat, sure the Potence 5 vampire may Botch the attack and end causing problems to himself, but don't count on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if the binded Wraith had a large Shadowland warband (Renegade Host who does not care for the Dictuum Mortium) at his disposal- say the Mage specifically sought to bind the Wraith for that very reason, what level of Construct/Installation could I take out? </div> </div> </div>Well, that looks<i> a lot </i>better than going solo.<br /> <br /> In a very general sense, if you bring numbers what ruins your day it's &quot;area of effect&quot; Procedures and Devices (well, that and, of course, enemy numbers). For instance, things like Wards can stop a warband as easily as a solo wraith (again, if I was the ST I would make some way to either disable the ward or allow a roll to bypass it, but your minions might not be able to pass...).<br /> <br /> While this depends on a lot of unknown factors, and thus I can't do more than guess, I would say a decent Wraith warband making a surprise attack should have a good chance against the average Construct, unless the Construct it's very focused on War and/or dealing with EDEs (in wich case several strong &quot;area of effect&quot; defenses, weapons and/or &quot;citizens&quot; with dangerous Devices are to be expected).<br /> <br /> The attack wants to be a fast &quot;hit and run&quot; tactic, so the Technocracy can't deploy massive anty-EDE weapons or a troop of VE marines on the place in time. Imagine attacking the Technocracy like robbing a bank with a band, you may be able to overpower the security of the bank but you don't want to be there when the police comes...and even if you <i>could </i>defeat the police, you <i>really</i> don't want to remain until the army arrives. It's not entirely impossible to make the Technocracy fold and cut their looses, but that's likely beyond what any reasonable warband would be able to accomplish<br /> <br /> If you get a few successes, security will increase and specialized teams will be sent to terminate your band (and the mage). Sounds like fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-08-2019, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T09:55:21-08:00","id":1351064,"title":"","content":"Also Primium isn't just aggravated damage. Though I don't think it would be much use against a wraith.<br /> <br /> Primium is basically Antimagic made into an impossibly indestructible metal. So it outright ignores magical defense and can be used to block or destroy spells.... But also can't be enchanted itself.<br /> <br /> It's why my Technocrat cyborg didn't have Primium countermeasures. Because he could do enlightened science himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T13:42:36-08:00","id":1352210,"title":"","content":"Lol my head cannon is that any Attempts to control a wraith though occult means only controls the Wraith. The Shadow is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}